agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/acceptance/release/runs/A4-post-cursor-topic-20260831/logs/A4-regression-scope.log:113:Use separate logical lanes for every independently reviewable protected-test partition, AC evidence partition, static/unit/integration/E2E/non-functional evidence set, implementation module or diff region, human-acceptance binding/run, external sandbox, exploratory result, production signal, and rollback control. These are categories, not a fixed lane count: split them further whenever inputs and conclusions are isolated. Reuse hash-identical accepted review results rather than launching duplicate lanes.
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/acceptance/release/runs/A4-post-cursor-topic-20260831/logs/A4-regression-scope.log-114-
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/acceptance/release/runs/A4-post-cursor-topic-20260831/logs/A4-regression-scope.log-115-Worker capacity changes waves only. Do not merge review lanes because they share a feature, layer, role, repository, deadline, reviewer, or output decision. Group only a proven `write-write`, `mutable-read-write`, `single-migration`, `single-generated-artifact`, or `inseparable-transaction` conflict, and record the exact resource-level reason. Read-only access to the same frozen source or evidence is parallel-safe.
